---
const siteUrl = Astro.site!.href;
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow" />
    <title>Quick Guide — Jauhar Website Manager</title>
    <style>
      * {
        box-sizing: border-box;
      }
      body {
        margin: 0;
        background: #faf8f2;
        color: #143829;
        font:
          17px/1.65 system-ui,
          sans-serif;
      }
      main {
        max-width: 760px;
        margin: auto;
        padding: 24px 20px 64px;
      }
      h1,
      h2 {
        font-family: Georgia, serif;
        line-height: 1.25;
      }
      h1 {
        font-size: clamp(30px, 6vw, 44px);
      }
      h2 {
        margin-top: 40px;
      }
      a {
        color: inherit;
        display: inline-block;
        min-height: 44px;
        padding: 8px 0;
      }
      a:focus-visible {
        outline: 2px solid #806d3e;
        outline-offset: 4px;
      }
      .note {
        padding: 16px 20px;
        border-left: 4px solid #806d3e;
        background: #f1e9d7;
      }
      li {
        margin-bottom: 10px;
      }
      ol {
        padding-left: 24px;
      }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main>
      <a href="/admin/">← Back to Website Manager</a>
      <h1>A quick guide to your website</h1>
      <p>
        Sign in with your own GitHub account. You can manage products, photos, stories, business
        information and page introductions from your phone.
      </p>
      <p class="note">
        <strong>Save → wait → check.</strong> Saving starts a website update. The public website usually
        updates in a few minutes. “Saved” does not mean the new version is already live. Use <a
          href={siteUrl}
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener">Visit website</a
        > to check the result.
      </p>
      <h2>Change a price or availability</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Open <strong>Products</strong> and choose the product.</li><li>
          Change <strong>Price in Ringgit (RM)</strong>, <strong>Sold per</strong>, or <strong
            >Availability</strong
          >.
        </li><li>
          Choose <strong>Published</strong> if it should appear on the website, then tap <strong
            >Save</strong
          >.
        </li><li>Wait for the update, then check the Products page.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        <strong>Unavailable</strong> keeps the product visible as “Out of stock”, or pauses bookings for
        a farm experience. <strong>Draft — hidden</strong> removes it from both Home and Products.
      </p>
      <h2>Add a product or farm photo</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>
          Choose <strong>Products</strong> or <strong>Farm Photos</strong>, then <strong>New</strong
          >.
        </li><li>
          Fill in the required fields. Choose <strong>Photo → Browse</strong> to upload from your phone.
          JPG, PNG, WebP and HEIC are accepted, up to 12 MB.
        </li><li>
          Write a short description of what is visible in the photo. Keep the main subject near the
          centre because the website crops photos to fit.
        </li><li>
          Keep <strong>Draft — hidden</strong> selected while preparing it. Once all required fields are
          complete, tap <strong>Save</strong>.
        </li><li>
          Use <strong>Preview</strong> to check the content and visibility. When ready, select
          <strong>Published</strong> and save again.
        </li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        Photos are resized automatically. Wait for processing to finish before saving, especially on
        an older phone. Home shows up to three published products selected with <strong
          >Show on Home</strong
        >, using their position numbers.
      </p>
      <h2>Write a farm story</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Open <strong>Farm Stories → New</strong>.</li><li>
          Add a title, short description, date and cover photo.
        </li><li>
          Write in <strong>Story</strong> using the formatting toolbar. The page already has its main
          title; use Heading 2 or Heading 3 inside your story.
        </li><li>
          Complete the required fields and save as a draft. Preview it, then select <strong
            >Published</strong
          > when ready.
        </li>
      </ol>
      <h2>Update contact details or opening hours</h2>
      <p>
        Open <strong>Business Information → Contact &amp; Opening Hours</strong>. Use digits only
        for WhatsApp, including the country code. Times use the 24-hour clock, such as 09:00 and
        17:00. These details update the contact page, links and search information together. Keep
        them consistent with your Google Business Profile.
      </p>
      <h2>Change a page introduction</h2>
      <p>
        Open <strong>Page Introductions</strong> and select the page. Edit its heading, introduction,
        cover photo or search description. Keep headings short for phone screens. The preview shows the
        content; check the full page after saving. Preview helps you review the fields. It does not reproduce
        the exact website design.
      </p>
      <h2>If something goes wrong</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Cannot sign in:</strong> use the GitHub account invited by the website owner. If the
          sign-in window expires, close it and sign in again.
        </li><li>
          <strong>Photo is rejected:</strong> choose a supported photo under 12 MB. If HEIC processing
          fails, export the photo as JPG.
        </li><li>
          <strong>Changes do not appear:</strong> wait a few minutes, refresh the public page, and check
          that Visibility is Published. If it still has not updated, ask the website owner to check the
          Vercel deployment.
        </li><li>
          <strong>Made a mistake:</strong> change the field back and save. GitHub keeps a history, so
          the website owner can restore an earlier version.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
